From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Audit Hub <audit-hub@audit-hub.invalid>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 18:10:07 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] feat(api): send the app's version, build and platform on
 every request

docs/RELEASES.md#minimum-supported-version asks the app to tell the API
which version sends each request, so a backend can refuse one it no
longer supports, but nothing sent it. Every request, public ones
included, now carries X-App-Version and X-App-Build (expo-application,
already a dependency) and X-App-Platform. createHttp takes the headers
as an option (a failure to read them never fails a request, and a
caller's own header wins), and setRequestHeaders lets an integration
add its own to them.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
